# Agent Orchestration

This project defines 8 agents in `.vibeops/agents/*.md`. Each agent stays **inside its own role**.

## Flow

```
User/PM
   │
   ▼
[orchestrator]  ── pick next TASK, invoke the right agent
   │
   ├──▶ [planner]    idea → docs/project/{00,01,02,07}
   ├──▶ [architect]  docs/project/{03,04}
   ├──▶ [builder]    code changes for one TASK
   ├──▶ [reviewer]   diff vs Acceptance Criteria
   ├──▶ [tester]     run Test Plan → Test Result
   ├──▶ [docs]       update 05-current-state / TASK Result / logs
   └──▶ [recovery]   rollback diagnosis (destructive work requires --confirm)
```

## Invocation

Use the VibeOps CLI to get an agent-specific prompt.

```
vibeops agent prompt <agent> <TASK-NNN>
vibeops task prompt <TASK-NNN> --agent <agent>
```

Paste the emitted markdown into Cursor chat as-is.

## Responsibility boundaries

- `builder` does not do `reviewer` work. Self-checks are fine; review is a separate invocation.
- `planner` does not write code. `architect` does not decide business logic.
- `docs` does not make code changes; it updates documents only.
- No agent works on **multiple TASKs at the same time**.

## Forbidden

- "This is not my role, but I will do it anyway" is not allowed. Invoke the appropriate agent instead.
- Arbitrarily editing agent definition files (`.vibeops/agents/*.md`) without a TASK.
